# Verification policy (speed vs CI noise)

## Precedence

This rule overrides **running** the full checklist in **`.cursor/rules/testing-verification.mdc`** and the **AGENTS.md** smoke list **during mid-task exploration**. It does **not** waive the **pre-push gate** below.

## Mid-task (default)

While still editing (user has **not** asked to commit/push/finish), the agent **may skip** running:

- `composer test` / `php artisan test`
- `php artisan routes:smoke`
- `migrate:fresh --seed` for QA (**never** on prod/stage — **`prod-db-no-destructive.mdc`**)
- `npm run build` / `npm test` solely as a verification gate
- discretionary browser / curl “prove it” checks

Optional: one short line that mid-task verification was deferred.

## Mandatory pre-push gate (autoagents / integration branch)

Before **`git push`** to **`autoagents`** (or **`AGENT_GIT_BRANCH`**) when the push includes **application** changes under any of:

- `app/`, `routes/`, `database/`, `config/`, `resources/js/`, `resources/views/`, `tests/`, `docker/`, root `composer.*`, Vite/`package.json` scripts that affect the app

the agent **must**:

1. Run **`composer test`** (CI-parity; prefer this over Docker-only `php artisan test`) and fix failures **before** push.
2. If `resources/js/` or Vite config changed: **`npm run build`** must succeed.
3. If routes/middleware changed: **`php artisan routes:smoke`** (no HTTP 500) when practical on this host.

**Docs / changelog / version-only** pushes (`CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/**`, `.cursor/**`, `autoagents/tasks/**`, `package.json` bump alone with no app code): may skip `composer test`, but still follow **push batching** below.

If the user explicitly asks for full verification earlier, follow **`.cursor/rules/testing-verification.mdc`**.

## Push batching (reduce GitHub Failed noise)

Stage CI **deploys** on every `autoagents` push. Overlapping deploys caused Docker name conflicts and red ❌ runs even when **Build & Test** passed.

Agents **must**:

1. Prefer **one push per logical task** (code + changelog + version bump in the same commit series, then a **single** `git push`).
2. **Do not** push a follow-up “changelog wording only” commit seconds after a deploy-triggering push — fold it into the same push, or wait until the previous Stage workflow finished / was cancelled.
3. Interactive Maestro/Cursor sessions: same rule — batch micro-commits locally; **one** push when the operator says go/commit/done.

Workflow concurrency (`stage.yml`) cancels in-progress Stage runs when a newer push arrives; still avoid spam pushes.

## Always: project version

Whenever tracked app/docs that ship change and work ends in **commit and/or push**, bump root semver with **`npm version patch --no-git-tag-version`** per **`.cursor/rules/agent-task-version-bump.mdc`**. No bump if no files changed.
